NAME
       pwconv - move passwords into the shadow file

SYNOPSIS
       pwconv

DESCRIPTION
       pwconv creates or updates /etc/shadow from /etc/passwd: password
       hashes found in /etc/passwd are moved to /etc/shadow and replaced by x.
       RHEL uses shadow passwords from installation, so it is needed only
       after someone edited the files by hand. pwunconv does the reverse;
       grpconv does the same for groups.

EXAMPLES
           pwconv
           pwck -r

SEE ALSO
       pwck(8), grpconv(8), shadow(5)
